{#
/**
 * @file
 * The global footer — ported from templates/news-b.html (byte-identical on
 * every template). Hand-authored Twig, not a block region. Its CONTENT is
 * the CMS's (icon_preprocess_page(), from icon_site): `footer` — the call
 * to action, its link, the newsletter line, the acknowledgement (Content →
 * Footer) and `footer.social` (the footer-social menu); `offices` — the
 * Office content in list order (Content → Offices), each with its Icon media
 * inlined. `footer_cache` carries their cache tags. The newsletter inputs
 * stay the visual spec of a future webform/newsletter block (see the
 * comment in the markup). The films inside the mark are theme assets
 * (assets/banner/).
 *
 * Behaviour: Drupal.behaviors.iconFooter (icon/site-footer) — replaying
 * reveal, one-video-at-a-time films, scroll-velocity skew.
 */
#}
{% set theme_path = base_path ~ directory %}
<footer class="site-footer{{ footer_contact ? ' site-footer--contact' }}" id="site-footer">
  {% if footer_contact %}
    {# THE CONTACT PAGE (icon_preprocess_page(), footer_contact): the CTA is
       the newsletter — LET'S TALK would invite the reader to the page they
       are on — and the body below is hidden by the modifier (the offices
       are open on the page). The words are the site's, not Content →
       Footer's, which keeps its newsletter blurb for the other pages. #}
    <div class="site-footer__cta site-footer__cta--newsletter">
      <h2 class="site-footer__talk"
        ><span class="site-footer__talk-line"><span class="site-footer__talk-word" style="--w: 0">{{ 'Join'|t }}</span></span>
        <span class="site-footer__talk-line"><span class="site-footer__talk-word" style="--w: 1">{{ 'our'|t }}</span></span><br />
        <span class="site-footer__talk-line"><span class="site-footer__talk-word" style="--w: 2">{{ 'newsletter'|t }}</span></span
      ></h2>
      <div class="site-footer__cta-subscribe">
        <div class="subscribe-bar subscribe-bar--footer" data-subscribe-bar>
          <span class="subscribe-bar__glyph" aria-hidden="true"><svg class="subscribe-bar__svg subscribe-bar__svg--mail" viewBox="2 4 20 16" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="3" y="5" width="18" height="14" rx="2" /><path d="m3 8 9 6 9-6" /></svg></span>
          <label class="sr-only" for="contact-footer-email">{{ 'Email address'|t }}</label>
          <span class="subscribe-bar__field">
            <input class="subscribe-bar__input" id="contact-footer-email" type="email" name="email" placeholder=" " autocomplete="email" data-subscribe-input>
            <span class="subscribe-bar__hint" aria-hidden="true"><span class="subscribe-bar__hint-rest">{{ 'Subscribe'|t }}</span><span class="subscribe-bar__hint-hover">{{ 'Your email'|t }}</span></span>
          </span>
          <button class="subscribe-bar__go" type="button" data-subscribe aria-label="{{ 'Subscribe'|t }}"><svg class="subscribe-bar__svg" viewBox="4 4 16 16" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M6 5v10h12" /><path d="m14 11 4 4-4 4" /></svg></button>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  {% else %}
  <h2 class="site-footer__cta">
    <a class="site-footer__cta-link" href="{{ footer.touch_url }}">
      <!-- Split per word only so each can rise out of its own mask; the
           space between the spans is real, so the link still reads
           "Let's talk Get in touch". -->
      <span class="site-footer__talk"
        >{% for word in footer.talk|split(' ') %}{% if not loop.first %} {% endif %}<span class="site-footer__talk-line"><span class="site-footer__talk-word" style="--w: {{ loop.index0 }}">{{ word }}</span></span>{% endfor %}</span>
      <span class="site-footer__touch invite-arrow">{{ footer.touch }}</span>
    </a>
  </h2>
  {% endif %}

  <div class="site-footer__body">
    <div class="site-footer__newsletter">
      <p class="site-footer__blurb">{{ footer.newsletter }}</p>
      <!-- No <form> yet, on purpose: the subscribe behaviour ships with
           the newsletter slice, and a form here would let Enter fire a
           phantom submit. Drupal: webform/newsletter block renders the
           real form; these two stay its visual spec. -->
      <div class="subscribe-bar subscribe-bar--footer" data-subscribe-bar>
        <span class="subscribe-bar__glyph" aria-hidden="true"><svg class="subscribe-bar__svg subscribe-bar__svg--mail" viewBox="2 4 20 16" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="3" y="5" width="18" height="14" rx="2" /><path d="m3 8 9 6 9-6" /></svg></span>
        <label class="sr-only" for="footer-email">{{ 'Email address'|t }}</label>
        <span class="subscribe-bar__field">
          <input class="subscribe-bar__input" id="footer-email" type="email" name="email" placeholder=" " autocomplete="email" data-subscribe-input>
          <span class="subscribe-bar__hint" aria-hidden="true"><span class="subscribe-bar__hint-rest">{{ 'Subscribe'|t }}</span><span class="subscribe-bar__hint-hover">{{ 'Your email'|t }}</span></span>
        </span>
        <button class="subscribe-bar__go" type="button" data-subscribe aria-label="{{ 'Subscribe'|t }}"><svg class="subscribe-bar__svg" viewBox="4 4 16 16" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M6 5v10h12" /><path d="m14 11 4 4-4 4" /></svg></button>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="site-footer__locations">
      <h3 class="sr-only">Our offices</h3>
      <ul class="site-footer__offices" role="list">
        {% for office in offices %}
          <li class="site-footer__office-item" data-rule="{{ loop.last ? 'both' : 'top' }}">
            <details class="site-footer__office">
              <summary class="site-footer__office-summary">
                {# the office's Icon media, inlined; fill follows currentColor #}
                {{ icon_inline_svg(office.icon, 'site-footer__office-icon') }}
                <span class="site-footer__office-city">{{ office.city }}</span>
                <span class="site-footer__office-place">{{ office.place }}</span>
                <span class="site-footer__office-toggle" aria-hidden="true"></span>
              </summary>
              <address class="site-footer__office-details">
                <p>{% for line in office.lines %}{% if not loop.first %}<br />{% endif %}{{ line }}{% endfor %}</p>
                {% if office.phone or office.email %}
                  <p class="site-footer__office-contact">{% if office.phone %}{{ 'Phone'|t }} <a href="{{ office.phone_href }}">{{ office.phone }}</a>{% endif %}{% if office.phone and office.email %}<br />{% endif %}{% if office.email %}<a href="mailto:{{ office.email }}">{{ office.email }}</a>{% endif %}</p>
                {% endif %}
              </address>
            </details>
          </li>
        {% endfor %}
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="site-footer__base">
    <ul class="site-footer__social" role="list">
      {% for link in footer.social %}
        <li><a class="site-footer__social-link" href="{{ link.url }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">{{ link.title }}</a></li>
      {% endfor %}
    </ul>
    <p class="site-footer__ack">{{ footer.acknowledgement }}</p>
  </div>

  <!-- The brand lockup closes every page: the ICON logo at full width, with
       the hero's banner films playing inside it (see site-footer.css — the
       mark is a mask over a fill layer, so its contents are swappable).
       One clean string for assistive tech; the mark itself is decorative.

       The films and stills are THE HOMEPAGE HERO'S OWN SLIDES (footer_slides
       from icon_preprocess_page(): the Hero slide content, in the hero's
       order), at the very same URLs the hero renders — the same image style
       for a still, the raw film for a video — so once the hero, or any
       earlier footer, has played one, the browser serves it from cache
       here rather than fetching it again. preload="none" (and loading=lazy
       on a still) is deliberate: nothing is fetched until js/site-footer.js
       starts the reel, which it only does once the panel is on screen, so
       a page that never scrolls to the footer costs nothing. The theme's
       two banner films are the fallback for a site with no slides yet. -->
  <p class="site-footer__lockup">
    <span class="sr-only">ICON</span>
    <span class="site-footer__lockup-line" aria-hidden="true">
      <span class="site-footer__logo">
        {% if footer_slides is not empty %}
          {% for slide in footer_slides %}
            {% if slide.source.type == 'video' %}
              <video class="site-footer__slide{{ loop.first ? ' is-current' }}" src="{{ slide.source.src }}"{% if slide.source.poster %} poster="{{ slide.source.poster }}"{% endif %} muted playsinline loop preload="none"></video>
            {% else %}
              <img class="site-footer__slide{{ loop.first ? ' is-current' }}" src="{{ slide.source.src }}" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async"{% if slide.source.width %} width="{{ slide.source.width }}"{% endif %}{% if slide.source.height %} height="{{ slide.source.height }}"{% endif %}>
            {% endif %}
          {% endfor %}
        {% else %}
          <video class="site-footer__slide is-current" src="{{ theme_path }}/assets/banner/NWMPHN.mp4" muted playsinline loop preload="none"></video>
          <video class="site-footer__slide" src="{{ theme_path }}/assets/banner/banner-vid-nike-mara.mp4" muted playsinline loop preload="none"></video>
        {% endif %}
      </span>
    </span>
  </p>
  {{ footer_cache }}
</footer>
